Paper 10-B – Soft Skills: Chapter 1, Module B-02 – Soft Skills-1, Empathy, Openness with Visitors and Victims, Clarity While Making Decisions, Empathetic Approach Towards Grievances, Definition and Difference Between Soft and Hard Skills, Importance of Soft Skills, Body Language, Handling Vulnerable Groups, Senior Citizens and Disabled Persons, Elements of Soft Skills – Written, Oral, Gestures, Signs and Expressions.

Paper 1 – BNSS: Chapter 1, Module A-1 – Introduction to Laws, BNSS Sections 63–83 (Summons and Warrants), Sections 84–86 (Proclamation and Attachment of Property) and Sections 94–97, 101–104 (Processes to Compel Production of Things, Search Warrants and General Provisions Relating to Searches).

Paper 2 – BNS: Chapter 7, Module A-06 – Crime Against Women, Dowry Death (Section 80), Cruelty by Relatives (Sections 85–86), Abetment of Suicide (Section 108). Chapter 5, Module A-04 – Missing Children and Human Trafficking (Sections 93–99 and Sections 137–146).

Paper 3 – Central Minor Acts and Special Laws: Chapter 1, Module A-01 – Introduction to Laws, Cigarettes and Other Tobacco Products Act, 2003 (Sections 1–3, 6, 12, 13, 21, 24, 27 and 28). Police Forces (Restriction of Rights) Act, 1966 (Sections 1–5). Chapter 2, Module A-02 – Preventive Measures, Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act, 1967 (Sections 2, 10, 13, 16, 38, 39, 40 and 45) and National Security Act, 1980 (Sections 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9 and 14).

